Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 3.1.1: the root rule (6.1) is no exemption from the
   value conditions -- a module's root class inherits Value like any other
   class does, so an identity method it defines is refused exactly as a
   nested class's would be. The refusal is decided once per application, by
   `Mutator::apply_mixin`, which runs for the root's application just as it
   does for a nested class's -- unlike the enclosing-object condition, which
   is decided where a class object is created and so needs `after_clause`,
   which the root never reaches. `run` instantiates the root before sending
   `main:args:`, so the method never runs. *)
class ValueModuleDefiningIdentity usingPlatform: platformAtCreation = Object <: Value () (
    public == other = ( ^false )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: 'ran'; newLine
    )
) : ()
